[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug, one fix queued. Its reports say three. The queued parser
fix leaves two of them open.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket now. Shipping the parser fix does not close #4471.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table places every report by its tenant. The note under it is the third problem: those
reports have no swapped month at all. Its last column predates the tickets below: `hint` has one now.

## The three problems

| problem | its reports | ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first; our tenants write the day first, so day and month swap. This is the fix that is queued. | the `parser` row, less the one-day moves noted under it | [issue #1](https://github.com/albertlillington-heliosx/mega-s01e03/issues/1) |
| `hint`: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, then reads the date day first. People type what the hint says. The parser fix does not reach these. | the `hint` row | [issue #2](https://github.com/albertlillington-heliosx/mega-s01e03/issues/2) |
| `one-day`: the date moves by one day, not by a month. Lisbon gets Tuesday, Toronto gets Monday. | the one-day moves noted under the table (`desk-notes.json`) | [issue #3](https://github.com/albertlillington-heliosx/mega-s01e03/issues/3) |

## How they were counted

- One id, one report: the export repeats some reports across its pages.
- A report's problem comes from its tenant (locale and booking form, `causes.ts`), not from the
  intake tag. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser, and an en-US browser in Lisbon is still Lisbon.
  Compare the "tagged as" column with the row it sits in.
- A report the desk read as a one-day move belongs to the one-day problem, not to the cause its
  tenant files it under.

## Lessons

- A matching subject line is not a matching cause ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  "Wrong day on the invite" covers all three problems.
- Read a sample of the bodies before marking a big ticket known.

